            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for a headache, then the Kannada for rest."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ದುಃಖ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ದುಃಖ (duḥkha) — \"sadness, sorrow\". The two small circles ಃ after ದು are the visarga: a breath at the end of the syllable, duḥ-kha."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is the opposite of ಸಂತೋಷ (santōṣa), \"happiness\", which you met at the start."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The other side of santōṣa."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
